    "body": "`GenerateReqInput.no_logs` is documented as the per-request opt-out of request\nlogging (\"Whether to disallow logging for this request (e.g. due to ZDR)\",\n`managers/io_struct.py`) and it is plumbed through to the internal\n`TokenizedGenerateReqInput`, but no code path ever reads it. A request that sets\n`no_logs=true` is still logged in full — at `--log-requests-level 3` the prompt\ntext and tokenized input end up in the request log.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nServe with `--log-requests --log-requests-level 3` and send\n`{\"text\": \"<prompt>\", \"no_logs\": true}` to `/generate`: the server still writes\n`Receive: obj=GenerateReqInput(..., text='<prompt>', ...)` and the matching\n`Finish: obj=...` records.\n\n## Fix\n\n`RequestLogger.log_received_request` / `log_finished_request` are the only paths\nthat emit request payloads, so both now skip a request that carries `no_logs`.\n`getattr(obj, \"no_logs\", False)` keeps request types that do not define the\nfield (`EmbeddingReqInput`) logging as before.\n\nScope: this only changes request logging. Debug/crash dumping\n(`dump_requests_folder`) is untouched — it is an explicit operator opt-in, while\n`no_logs` is the per-request contract.\n\n## Test\n\nNew CPU-only `test/registered/unit/utils/test_request_logger.py`:\n\n- `no_logs=true` writes nothing for received or finished requests (both fail\n  against unpatched `main`, verified)\n- `no_logs=false` still logs the request content\n- a request type without the field still logs\n\nDuplicates: no open PR or issue touches `no_logs` or this logging gate (checked\nPRs/issues and code search at main before writing this).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37215745048](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37215745048)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37215744912](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37215744912)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37215745120](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37215745120)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
